</section>
<section id="S11" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">11 </span>Additional baselines and deeper networks</h2>

<div id="S11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We pretrain <span id="S11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Strainer</span> using <math id="S11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> images (<math id="S11.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="100\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100\times</annotation></semantics></math> than <span id="S11.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Snp</span> and <span id="S11.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Strainer</span>), each randomly selected from a different class to ensure spectral coverage, for <math id="S11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> epochs using the best model for image fitting. Table <a href="#S11.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ 11 Additional baselines and deeper networks ‣ The Surprising Effectiveness of Noise Pretraining for Implicit Neural Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows <span id="S11.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Snp</span>: Spectrum outperforming <span id="S11.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Strainer</span>: ImageNet, indicating the crucial role of <math id="S11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/f</annotation></semantics></math> prior directly encoded through spectrum noise. Table <a href="#S11.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ 11 Additional baselines and deeper networks ‣ The Surprising Effectiveness of Noise Pretraining for Implicit Neural Representations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows <span id="S11.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Snp</span> also generalizes to deeper 10-layer INRs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S11.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S11.T9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 9</span>: </span><span id="S11.T9.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Fitting results<span id="S11.T9.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> on additional baselines and deeper INRs.</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="S11.T9.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:243.5pt;height:87.6pt;vertical-align:-41.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-30.4pt,11.0pt) scale(0.8,0.8) ;">
